# Repository-root ignores.
#
# bronze_layer/.gitignore already covers these, but only relative to
# bronze_layer/. CI runs pytest with `working-directory: bronze_layer`, so
# the artifacts land there and are ignored. Running the same suite from the
# repository root - `pytest bronze_layer/tests` - puts them HERE instead,
# where nothing was ignoring them, and a `git add -A` will happily commit
# several MB of Delta parquet. Duplicated deliberately rather than moved:
# both working directories are legitimate.

# Local pytest run artifacts: the Delta-backed tests spin up a real local
# Spark session, which materializes test tables under spark-warehouse/ and,
# depending on session config, a Derby metastore alongside it. All of it is
# regenerated on demand and must never be committed.
spark-warehouse/
metastore_db/
derby.log

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Packaging
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Databricks CLI / bundle local state
.databricks/

# Local virtualenvs. `.venv311` is the Python 3.11 environment CONTRIBUTING
# describes for running the Spark-backed tests on Windows (#74) - several
# hundred MB of pyspark, and per-developer by nature.
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
